From 3a1b81800a55f77df34677ef09ecf91db09268f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:17:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] ##arch: Emulate the USSE forms of the fifth probe round

A fifth round of client fills on an SGX545 pinned the integer
multiply-add modes, the shift amounts the earlier rounds left out, the
Pn predicate and the dual-issue pairs that share a unit, and the ESIL
follows:

- shl/shr/asr/rol: an immediate amount of 32 and over acts as a register
  one, and ~ complements a register or immediate amount first
- Pn (predicate value 7) never runs the instruction
- idiv d, a, b: the unsigned quotient to d and the remainder to d + 1,
  all ones to both for a zero divisor
- imae: .usat/.ssat saturate, .rsN shifts the sum right, a u16 source 2
  is sign-extended and a z16 one zero-extended, coe writes the carry out
  to iN and cie adds iN; ima32's cie adds iN
- ima16 with u8, s8 and o8 sources: the .low/.high byte of each lane's
  half, o8 being the byte minus 128; .rsN on the unsigned forms
- ima8: x + y * z per byte from the selectors, wrapping or with .sat
  clamped to 255
- dual issue: ima32 as a secondary computes two 16-bit lanes and takes
  the primary's source 1 as b after fmad/fadm/fmsa/fssq; a multiplying
  secondary of fadm/fmsa/fssq gets the primary's second product, an
  fmsa one of fmad/fadm/fmsa and an ima32 one of ima32 the primary's
  result, fadd/fsub/fmad after fminmax max(a, b) - c

Also bank-7 numbers past i3 lose their ESIL: they read the other pixels
of the 2x2 quad and drop writes, which one emulated instance cannot do.

Not modelled: the sampler, fmad16 and the c10 colour operands, usat with
a sign-extended source 2, fmad + fmad16 and fmad + fmaxmin.

14 new and 3 changed test/db/esil/usse tests. The microkernel uses none
of these forms: 84.2% of its words still have ESIL; 725 of 153466
decodable random words do (was 662).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
